{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 22, :comments ["<b>You shall not delay to fulfill it, etc.</b> Because a person's evil inclination has its strength specifically in a vowed matter, and all the while that his vow rests upon him the evil inclination battles him all the more, and says to him: Is it not enough for you what the Torah has forbidden you? Come and do not add to it, to multiply the provocations of the evil inclination within you — therefore it is said: ״לֹא תְאַחֵר לְשַׁלְּמוֹ״, that you should not stand many days in its snare. And therefore it is said: ״וְכִי תֶחְדַּל לִנְדֹּר לֹא יִהְיֶה בְךָ חֵטְא״, that is, the evil inclination that causes you to sin; but if you delay to fulfill it, then HaShem will surely require it of you, and whatever the Holy One, blessed be He, requires of you — the evil inclination incites you not to attend to it; therefore ״וְהָיָה בְךָ חֵטְא״ for certain, for this evil inclination will find an opening to battle against you and say: This matter carries no absolute obligation upon you — is it for the sake of some empty word that there should be an obligation upon you to do it? And after this he will come to incite him and to mislead him also away from the other commandments of HaShem. And what is written: ״וְהָיָה בְךָ חֵטְא״ — this is like what our Rabbis of blessed memory said (Shabbat 105a): ״לֹא יִהְיֶה בְךָ אֵל זָר״ — this is the evil inclination. And the commandment of ״לֹא יִהְיֶה בְךָ״ means that you should not provoke him within yourself." "Another matter: if you delay to fulfill it, because it is evil in your eyes to diminish from your money, then know that HaShem will surely require it of you — from another place, and He will cause you to lose just as much money according to the value of the vow, and the impression of the sin will be upon you, and also the money you will not profit from, and you will lose it from another place."], :book :deuteronomy, :voice :kli-yakar, :lang :en, :chapter 23, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-30T13:13:32.606287369Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}